A||||4||Ted||Placement of tires
Z||000000||Ted||08-15-99||10:27 AM||||My rear tires are getting close to bald. I was wondering if it is better to have these tires in the front or the back?<br>
Z||000001||batboy||08-15-99||11:01 AM||||Leave em on the rear. You want good tires up front so you can steer. Please get some better tires soon. Bad tires hydroplane easily (read the post on hydroplaning).
Z||000002||Ted||08-15-99||09:59 PM||||Thanx batboy. I read the planing article
Z||000003||Patrick||08-15-99||11:31 PM||||<br>I agree with batboy. I tried using my balder tires up front, and yes, it was rather disconcerting to turn the steering wheel and then continue to go in a straight line while driving on a wet road.<p><p>
Z||000004||lowCG||08-16-99||12:52 AM||||Yeah,then after the front smushes,and slides around around,it'll hook-up just enough to whip the tail out,and you'll have no chance to recover.<br>If you never see rain,the bald tires work pretty good,still would want them on the back though.<br>Hey,Firestone has a 90 days-same-as-cash-deal on all their tires,a set of RE71s would really make difference over the stock-type tires...
